"derive:instance_mirror over a whole store: instanceOf declares Person an ObjectType, one role fact says Person plays position 1 of fact type F1, and F1 holds two rows. Every id at that position is therefore an instance of Person. -two-nouns is the join doing real work -- one fact type, TWO roles played by different nouns at different positions, so the column read differs per role and the answer must pair each id with the noun whose role it played, not with both. -no-nouns pins the arm where the role player is not an entity, which must derive nothing rather than pair against a value type.",
