"A NOUN SEES ITS OWN MACHINES AND A COMPOSITE STATUS BEHAVES AS HAREL SAYS (2026-09-09). Ticket's machine starts at New; `start` enters Open, a nested machine whose initial is A, where `advance` goes to B; `close` is from Open to Closed. Note's machine has a status named A too, with `publish`. The Ticket table holds start, close and advance and the inherited row that close is from A and from B -- and no publish; the Note table holds publish alone. A started ticket stands at A, Open's leaf initial, not at Open; started and closed it stands at Closed, because close is from Open and A is inside Open; and its links at A offer advance and close both.",
