"AND A POPULATION CAN BE READ BACK. GET answered Theorem 2-s nav leg and no method returned ROWS, so the MCP surface could POST into any of 246 fact types and query none of them. The fillers restrict by PREFIX and both edges fall out of theta:zip rather than a branch: zip truncates to the shorter side, so one filler against a two-column row compares role 1 and ignores role 2, and an EMPTY filler zips to nothing while fp:and_all of nothing is T, so a bare read matches every row. Codd-s theta-restriction with the identity restriction as its zero case. The third one is the case that matters -- a filler nobody holds answers nothing rather than falling back to the whole population, which is the shape a read like this fails in.",
